From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Om Swami <reach.oms2004@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:44:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(mintv2): note keys from a provider, and notes issued
 to external keys

`NoteKeyProvider` supplies each note's spend key and blinding key.
`MintClientInit` derives them from the module root secret as before;
`MintClientInitWithKeys` takes a provider whose spend keys an external
signer holds. Wallet notes carry a local or remote spend key, and remote
ones are spent through the client's transaction signer. Such a wallet only
spends notes when a transaction needs funding, so receiving stays signed by
the client alone, and it refuses to hand out bearer e-cash itself.

`issue_external_notes` issues notes to nonces and blinding keys the caller
provides and returns their signatures without adding them to the wallet;
`claim_external_notes` spends such notes back into the wallet.

The client database encoding of notes changes, without a migration yet.
